    "details": "The ImageMagick project published security advisories for issues fixed\nin releases 6.9.13-51 through 6.9.13-59. They include heap buffer\noverflows, use-after-free, out-of-bounds reads, integer overflows,\ndivision by zero, memory leaks and security policy bypasses in various\ncoders. A crafted image file can crash the process, disclose memory\ncontents or circumvent the configured security policy.\n",
